---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const siteTitle = "How to Connect Windsurf IDE to Browser MCP for Agent Browsing • BrowserReviews";
const siteDescription = "Complete setup guide for connecting Windsurf IDE (Codeium) to 2Captcha Browser MCP via ~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json. Grant Cascade autonomous web browsing and anti-bot bypass.";

const schemaMarkup = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Connect Windsurf IDE & Cascade to Browser MCP for Autonomous Web Browsing",
  "description": "Configure mcp_config.json in Windsurf IDE to give Cascade AI Agent full browser navigation, DOM inspection, and automated anti-bot bypass capabilities.",
  "totalTime": "PT4M",
  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Locate Windsurf MCP Configuration File",
      "text": "Open ~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json (on macOS/Linux: ~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json; on Windows: %USERPROFILE%/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json)."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Add 2Captcha Browser MCP Server Configuration",
      "text": "Add the twocaptcha-browser entry to the mcpServers object with your API key."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Refresh Cascade MCP Tools in Windsurf",
      "text": "Open Cascade in Windsurf, click the Hammer/Tool icon or reload the window to verify available browser actions."
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4,
      "name": "Execute Web Automation via Cascade Prompts",
      "text": "Instruct Cascade to navigate to URLs, extract live tables, audit competitors, or bypass Turnstile verification."
    }
  ]
};

const jsonSnippet = JSON.stringify({
  mcpServers: {
    "twocaptcha-browser": {
      command: "npx",
      args: ["-y", "@2captcha/browser-mcp"],
      env: {
        TWOCAPTCHA_API_KEY: "your_2captcha_api_key_here"
      }
    }
  }
}, null, 2);
---

<Base title={siteTitle} description={siteDescription}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schemaMarkup)} />

  <article class="guide-container">
    <div class="guide-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides">Guides</a> / <span>Windsurf Browser MCP</span>
      </div>
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="pill pill-gold">Windsurf IDE / Cascade</span>
        <span class="pill">MCP Guide</span>
        <span class="pill">4 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1>How to Connect Windsurf IDE to Browser MCP for Agent Browsing</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Windsurf (by Codeium) features <strong>Cascade</strong>, an AI coding agent with deep context awareness. By pairing Windsurf with the <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> and the <strong>2Captcha Browser MCP</strong> server, Cascade gains a full cloud browser engine capable of scraping live websites, testing frontend apps, and bypassing Cloudflare Turnstile barriers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-body">
      <h2>Why Connect Windsurf Cascade to a Cloud Browser MCP?</h2>
      <p>
        While Cascade can write and edit code in your repository, it has no native window into dynamic web content. Standard HTTP fetch tools fail on modern React/Vue SPAs and get blocked instantly by Cloudflare, DataDome, or Akamai firewalls.
      </p>
      <p>
        Connecting Windsurf to <strong>2Captcha Browser MCP</strong> unlocks:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dynamic JavaScript Execution:</strong> Cascade inspects rendered DOM trees, client-rendered tables, and interactive elements.</li>
        <li><strong>Automated CAPTCHA &amp; WAF Solving:</strong> Turnstile and reCAPTCHA challenges are resolved automatically in the cloud before content reaches Cascade.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero Local Chrome Overhead:</strong> Browser instances run on high-performance cloud nodes with clean residential IP routing, keeping your developer machine cool and quiet.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Step 1: Locate or Create Windsurf's MCP Config</h2>
      <p>
        Windsurf manages external MCP servers through a single configuration file named <code>mcp_config.json</code> located in your user profile:
      </p>
      <div class="os-paths">
        <p><strong>macOS &amp; Linux:</strong> <code>~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json</code></p>
        <p><strong>Windows:</strong> <code>%USERPROFILE%\.codeium\windsurf\mcp_config.json</code> (or <code>C:\Users\&lt;You&gt;\.codeium\windsurf\mcp_config.json</code>)</p>
      </div>
      <p>
        You can also open this directly from Windsurf by pressing <code>Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + P</code> and selecting <strong>Preferences: Open User Settings (JSON)</strong> or navigating to Windsurf Settings &gt; Model Context Protocol.
      </p>

      <h2>Step 2: Add 2Captcha Browser MCP Server Entry</h2>
      <p>
        Add the <code>twocaptcha-browser</code> server definition inside the <code>mcpServers</code> object. If <code>mcp_config.json</code> already has other tools (e.g. Postgres, GitHub), simply append this block:
      </p>
      <pre class="code-block"><code>{jsonSnippet}</code></pre>
      <p>
        Replace <code>your_2captcha_api_key_here</code> with your active 2Captcha API key from your dashboard.
      </p>

      <h2>Step 3: Refresh Cascade &amp; Verify MCP Tools</h2>
      <p>
        Save <code>mcp_config.json</code> and restart Windsurf, or press <code>Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + P</code> and run <strong>Developer: Reload Window</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open the Cascade panel. You will now see active browser automation tools registered under MCP:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>browser_navigate</code>: Instructs the cloud browser to open any URL with automated WAF solving.</li>
        <li><code>browser_snapshot</code>: Captures the rendered DOM tree, text nodes, and computed styles.</li>
        <li><code>browser_click</code>: Clicks buttons, dropdowns, and triggers client-side events.</li>
        <li><code>browser_screenshot</code>: Returns full-page PNG captures for UI verification.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Step 4: Example Cascade Prompts</h2>
      <p>
        In Cascade agent mode, you can now execute end-to-end browser workflows:
      </p>
      <div class="prompt-box">
        <p><strong>Competitor Research:</strong> "Navigate to https://example-store.com/new-releases, bypass any Cloudflare challenges, and extract all product titles, SKUs, and prices into a JSON file."</p>
        <p><strong>Frontend Verification:</strong> "Open http://localhost:3000/dashboard using the cloud browser, verify whether the metrics chart loaded, and take a screenshot."</p>
        <p><strong>Documentation Scrape:</strong> "Navigate to https://api.docs-vendor.com, expand the Authentication section, and draft a TypeScript API wrapper based on the rendered specs."</p>
      </div>

      <h2>#1 Recommended Browser MCP Provider</h2>
      <div class="gold-box">
        <div class="gold-header">
          <h3>2Captcha Browser MCP</h3>
          <span class="gold-badge">Rank #1 Best Overall</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          2Captcha Browser MCP is the gold standard for developer AI environments. Built-in Cloudflare Turnstile and reCAPTCHA solving, residential IP pools in 220+ countries, and true pay-as-you-go pricing ($0.05/hour) with zero recurring subscriptions.
        </p>
        <a href="https://2captcha.com/?from=browserreviews" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored" class="btn btn-gold">
          Get 2Captcha Browser API Key &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide-container {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }
  .guide-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e5e7eb);
  }
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted, #6b7280);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .badge-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .pill {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: var(--surface-secondary, #f3f4f6);
    color: var(--text-muted, #4b5563);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .pill-gold {
    background: #fef3c7;
    color: #92400e;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted, #4b5563);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .guide-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 2.2rem 0 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .guide-body p, .guide-body ul, .guide-body ol {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-primary, #1f2937);
  }
  .code-block {
    background: #0f172a;
    color: #f8fafc;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .os-paths {
    background: var(--surface-secondary, #f9fafb);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e5e7eb);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .os-paths p {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .prompt-box {
    background: #f0fdf4;
    border: 1px solid #bbf7d0;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .prompt-box p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    color: #166534;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .gold-box {
    background: #fffbeb;
    border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .gold-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .gold-header h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #92400e;
  }
  .gold-badge {
    background: #f59e0b;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
  }
  .gold-box p {
    color: #78350f;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .btn-gold {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #d97706;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-gold:hover {
    background: #b45309;
  }
</style>
